h is that  we are in a competitive global  environment a number of these countries  that are developing fast are becoming as  I say increasingly influential on the  world stage not just economically but  but uh you know politically  um  what's the word I'm looking for um  diplomatically  are being wooed  they are being they have choices and  either we find a way of encouraging  those countries to move in the direction  that we think is the right direction uh  increase openness  increase you know reform within  themselves as we are doing with Saudi  Arabia and others or we can choose to  detach but those countries will still be  influential those countries will still  be important but those countries will  increasingly increasingly be detached  from us I don't think that's in their  interest I certainly don't think it's in  the UK's National interest so we work  with we work with countries and when we  have disagreements we highlight those  disagreements where we have  opportunities to exert influence we seek  to reserve influence as well what about  Egypt a few weeks ago the uh sister of  Allah Abdel fatah the British Egyptian  political prisoner who's held there made  an appeal to the British prime minister  on this program uh to try and get her  brother's release what progress have you  made well the Prime Minister uh spoke  with President CeCe on this issue I've  spoken with the Egyptian foreign  minister on this I know our officials  speak with Egyptian officials on this  regularly as well so we are working we  continue to work on these Consular cases  both in Egypt and and elsewhere we we we  want to make sure that we  um have access to this person who is a  dual Egyptian British national will keep  working  um and sometimes these conversations  done publicly often they are done  privately but I can assure you in the  viewers that we continue working on this  there haven't been any specific  diplomatic consequences have there well  as I say we we do continue to